WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.848
Henry, Maggie, and Cole walked over to the picnic tables.

2
00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:22.844
People from a local restaurant were passing out snacks and drinks.

3
00:00:22.845 --> 00:00:27.326
Henry took a bottle of water, but he felt too worried to eat a snack.

4
00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:33.371
What if The Lemonade Detectives couldn't solve this case before the end of the ride?

5
00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:37.610
So far they'd done everything detectives were supposed to do.

6
00:00:37.611 --> 00:00:41.574
They'd figured out suspects, motives, and alibis.

7
00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:44.284
But they still hadn't solved the case.

8
00:00:44.285 --> 00:00:49.840
"Let's split up and question our last two suspects," Henry told his friends.

9
00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:54.937
"Okay," Cole agreed. "I'll try to talk to the mystery man if you want."

10
00:00:54.938 --> 00:00:58.052
"Fine. Maggie and I will find William."

11
00:00:58.053 --> 00:01:03.568
They split up and started searching. The picnic area was crowded.

12
00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:07.384
At first Henry didn't see either of their suspects.

13
00:01:07.385 --> 00:01:11.361
Then Maggie grabbed his arm. "There's William."

14
00:01:11.362 --> 00:01:14.281
Henry looked toward where she was pointing.

15
00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:19.520
William was sitting by himself, staring out at the woods and eating an apple.

16
00:01:19.521 --> 00:01:24.581
"Let's decide what we're going to say before we go over," Henry said.

17
00:01:24.582 --> 00:01:28.454
"We don't have time," Maggie said impatiently.

18
00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:33.918
"Let's just go tell him we know he did it. If he's guilty, he might confess."

19
00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:37.817
"I'm not sure that will work." Henry glanced at William.

20
00:01:37.818 --> 00:01:40.657
The new boy looked bored and lonely.

21
00:01:40.658 --> 00:01:45.295
Even though William was a suspect, Henry felt a little sorry for him.

22
00:01:45.296 --> 00:01:48.192
It couldn't be easy being the new kid in town.

23
00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:52.620
"Look, his bag is on the table behind him," Maggie said.

24
00:01:52.621 --> 00:01:54.619
"Come on, I have a plan!"

25
00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.285
"A plan? What is it?" Henry felt worried.

26
00:01:58.286 --> 00:02:04.854
Maggie wasn't usually the type of person who came up with logical, well-thought-out plans.

27
00:02:04.855 --> 00:02:09.897
She was the type of person who acted first and thought about it later.

28
00:02:09.898 --> 00:02:13.427
"There's no time to explain," Maggie said.

29
00:02:13.428 --> 00:02:18.296
"Just talk to him to distract him, and I'll take care of the rest."

30
00:02:18.297 --> 00:02:21.064
"Maggie, wait!" Henry said.

31
00:02:21.065 --> 00:02:22.746
It was too late.

32
00:02:22.747 --> 00:02:27.208
Maggie was already rushing toward the picnic table where William was sitting.

33
00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:32.090
Henry followed, hoping that her plan would work, whatever it was.

34
00:02:32.091 --> 00:02:35.072
William looked up when he saw them coming.

35
00:02:35.073 --> 00:02:38.141
He didn't look particularly happy to see them.

36
00:02:38.142 --> 00:02:41.542
"Hi," Henry said, trying to sound friendly.

37
00:02:41.543 --> 00:02:45.308
"That apple looks good. Where did you get it?"

38
00:02:45.309 --> 00:02:50.757
"Over there," William said, pointing to a basket that the restaurant people had set out.

39
00:02:50.758 --> 00:02:54.908
"Oh . . . great . . ." Henry was running out of things to say.

40
00:02:54.909 --> 00:02:58.126
He shot a desperate look at Maggie.

41
00:02:58.127 --> 00:03:01.612
She flopped down on the bench across from William.

42
00:03:01.613 --> 00:03:07.532
"Whew!" she exclaimed dramatically. "I'm so tired!"

43
00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:09.484
She flung her arms out.

44
00:03:09.485 --> 00:03:13.507
One knocked into William's unzipped bag and sent it flying.

45
00:03:13.508 --> 00:03:16.298
The contents scattered everywhere.

46
00:03:16.299 --> 00:03:21.491
"Hey!" William exclaimed. "You spilled all my stuff!"

47
00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:25.936
"Sorry," Maggie said, leaping down and grabbing the bag.

48
00:03:25.937 --> 00:03:28.044
She shook it upside down.

49
00:03:28.045 --> 00:03:33.198
"Oops, you're right. Everything fell out! But don't worry, I'll clean it up."

50
00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:37.471
Henry and William watched as she picked up all the spilled items.

51
00:03:37.472 --> 00:03:42.554
There was a cell phone, a house key, and a few other things.

52
00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:46.751
"There." Maggie zipped the bag shut. "All fixed."

53
00:03:46.752 --> 00:03:52.623
"Thanks," William muttered. "Um, did you guys want to sit here, or what?"

54
00:03:52.624 --> 00:03:59.870
"Maybe later," Maggie said. "Come on, Henry. Let's go find Cole."

55
00:03:59.871 --> 00:04:03.110
The two of them made their escape.

56
00:04:03.111 --> 00:04:08.736
"What was that all about?" Henry asked as soon as they were out of William's earshot.

57
00:04:08.737 --> 00:04:12.646
Maggie smiled. "Don't you get it?

58
00:04:12.647 --> 00:04:17.312
There was nothing in that bag that William could have used to slash the tires.

59
00:04:17.313 --> 00:04:23.721
And his bike shorts don't have pockets, so he couldn't be carrying a penknife or anything that way."

60
00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:27.537
"I suppose you're right," Henry agreed.

61
00:04:27.538 --> 00:04:33.189
"But how do you know he didn't drop the crime weapon in the woods after he used it?"

62
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:38.148
Maggie's face fell. "I didn't think of that." She frowned.

63
00:04:38.149 --> 00:04:41.109
"Why do you always have to be so logical?"

64
00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:45.836
"Never mind. It was still a pretty good plan," Henry said.

65
00:04:45.837 --> 00:04:49.794
"If there had been a penknife in there, it would've worked."

66
00:04:49.795 --> 00:04:53.489
"That's true." Maggie looked a little happier.

67
00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:57.133
"So should we go back and try to talk to William some more?"

68
00:04:57.134 --> 00:05:02.481
Before Henry could answer, he saw Cole rushing toward them, looking excited.

69
00:05:02.482 --> 00:05:06.085
"Big news!" he cried when he reached them.

70
00:05:06.086 --> 00:05:09.559
"Did you talk to the mystery man?" Henry asked.

71
00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:14.426
Cole shook his head. "I never found him," he said breathlessly.

72
00:05:14.427 --> 00:05:19.218
"But I did find out more about him. And about William too."

73
00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:22.947
"Really?" Maggie said. "Like what?"

74
00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:27.129
"Like William's family isn't just rich," Cole said.

75
00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.682
"His dad works for the government.

76
00:05:29.683 --> 00:05:33.172
He's a senator in the United States Senate!"

77
00:05:33.173 --> 00:05:38.088
"Really?" Henry said. "Wow. That's cool."

78
00:05:38.089 --> 00:05:42.276
Cole nodded. "But that's not all," he said.

79
00:05:42.277 --> 00:05:46.462
"Everyone has noticed that the mystery man follows William everywhere.

80
00:05:46.463 --> 00:05:52.148
What if he's planning to kidnap William and hold him for ransom?"
